# install.sh regenerates AGENTS.md (generic-agent mirror of CLAUDE.md) on every run — generated artifact, not tracked.
# Anchored to repo root so it does NOT also ignore nested files like plugin/commands/agents.md
# (git matches case-insensitively on macOS, so an unanchored rule swallowed the plugin command).
/AGENTS.md
# gen-plugin.sh output — generated build artifact, not tracked
dist/
# Local strategy artifacts under the otherwise-tracked research/ dir — keep off the public repo (cf. plans/, projects/)
research/2026-07-agent-audit.md
research/2026-07-portfolio-audit.md
research/2026-07-frontier-hunt-v2/
# Third-party agent-skill installers drop content here. The Neon skills that lived
# under these paths were REMOVED 2026-08-27: they taught direct Neon CLI/MCP workflows
# with zero awareness of scripts/cast-neon.sh, which deliberately wires the MCP
# read-only and gates branch-delete behind CAST_NEON_BRANCH_DELETE_OK — so an agent
# loading them was being coached around a fail-closed destructive-op guard.
# The ignore rules stay: they keep any future `skills add` content out of the tracked
# skill count (`git ls-files 'skills/*'`, scripts/cast-stats-lib.sh:42) rather than
# silently moving it. Both rules are intentionally unanchored: `.agents/` should match
# wherever a skills installer creates it, not only at the repo root.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
